    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0440" n="1230" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">460.509/7–1654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Embassy in the United Kingdom</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d125-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-16T16:30:00-04:00">July 16, 1954—4:30
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. Excon. For Stassen from Dulles. Regarding
                    timing for implementing decontrol items in my view the situation upon which the
                        NSC decision was based remains the same. I
                    believe that actual decontrol should be deferred and that the situation at
                    Geneva is such that we can set no definite future date. Recognize British may
                    react strongly against our position but we would be subject here to heavy
                    criticism if we make concessions on this issue prior to a definitive result at
                    Geneva. This would appear to be giving away our trump card before the game had
                    started. If you feel our position will result in serious breach with British in
                        CG meeting we can discuss matter further on
                    your return.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d125-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d125-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram, drafted by Goodkind and cleared by Roderic O’Connor, was repeated
                    to Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
